menu "Boot Configuration"

config STM32_ENABLE_FPU
    bool "Enable FPU (Floating Point Unit)"
    default y
    depends on STM32F4 || STM32F7 || STM32H7
    help
      Enable the Floating Point Unit (FPU) during system initialization.
      The FPU provides hardware acceleration for floating-point operations.

      Available on:
      - STM32F4 series (Cortex-M4F)
      - STM32F7 series (Cortex-M7F)
      - STM32H7 series (Cortex-M7F)

      When enabled, the FPU coprocessors (CP10 and CP11) are granted
      full access during SystemInit().

config STM32_STACK_SIZE
    hex "Stack size (bytes)"
    default 0x1000
    range 0x400 0x10000
    help
      Stack size in bytes for the main stack.
      Default: 0x1000 (4KB)
      Minimum: 0x400 (1KB)
      Maximum: 0x10000 (64KB)

      The stack is used for:
      - Function call frames
      - Local variables
      - Interrupt service routines

      Increase this value if you experience stack overflow or use
      deeply nested function calls.

config STM32_HEAP_SIZE
    hex "Heap size (bytes)"
    default 0x1000
    range 0x400 0x10000
    help
      Heap size in bytes for dynamic memory allocation.
      Default: 0x1000 (4KB)
      Minimum: 0x400 (1KB)
      Maximum: 0x10000 (64KB)

      The heap is used for:
      - malloc() and free() operations
      - C++ new and delete operators
      - Dynamic data structures

      Increase this value if you use dynamic memory allocation
      extensively in your application.

config STM32_ENABLE_CCM
    bool "Enable CCM RAM usage"
    default y
    depends on STM32F4 || STM32F7
    help
      Enable Core Coupled Memory (CCM) RAM usage.
      CCM is a fast SRAM region that is not accessible by DMA.

      Available on:
      - STM32F4 series (64KB at 0x10000000)
      - STM32F7 series (varies by model)

      When enabled, you can place data in CCM using:
        __attribute__((section(".ccmram"))) int my_data;

      Note: CCM cannot be used for DMA buffers.

config STM32_ENABLE_DTCM
    bool "Enable DTCM RAM usage"
    default y
    depends on STM32F7 || STM32H7
    help
      Enable Data Tightly Coupled Memory (DTCM) RAM usage.
      DTCM provides zero wait-state access for the CPU.

      Available on:
      - STM32F7 series (64KB at 0x20000000)
      - STM32H7 series (128KB at 0x20000000)

      DTCM is typically used for stack, heap, and frequently
      accessed variables.

config STM32_ENABLE_ITCM
    bool "Enable ITCM RAM usage"
    default n
    depends on STM32F7 || STM32H7
    help
      Enable Instruction Tightly Coupled Memory (ITCM) RAM usage.
      ITCM provides zero wait-state instruction fetch.

      Available on:
      - STM32F7 series (16KB at 0x00000000)
      - STM32H7 series (64KB at 0x00000000)

      When enabled, you can place time-critical code in ITCM:
        __attribute__((section(".itcmram"))) void fast_function(void);

      Note: Requires special linker script configuration.

config STM32_VTOR_OFFSET
    hex "Vector table offset"
    default 0x00000000
    help
      Offset of the vector table from the base address.
      Default: 0x00000000 (no offset)

      This is typically 0x00000000 for applications running from
      Flash start address (0x08000000).

      Set a non-zero value if:
      - Using a bootloader (e.g., 0x00008000 for 32KB bootloader)
      - Running from RAM
      - Using custom memory layout

config STM32_BOOT_TIMEOUT
    int "Boot timeout (ms)"
    default 100
    range 10 5000
    help
      Maximum time allowed for boot initialization in milliseconds.
      Default: 100ms

      This timeout applies to:
      - Clock configuration
      - HAL library initialization
      - Platform initialization

      If initialization takes longer than this timeout, the system
      will enter error handling mode.

config STM32_ENABLE_BOOT_LOGGING
    bool "Enable boot logging"
    default y if DEBUG
    default n
    help
      Enable logging output during boot process.
      Useful for debugging boot issues.

      When enabled, the boot process will output:
      - Clock configuration status
      - HAL initialization status
      - Platform initialization status
      - Error messages if initialization fails

      Automatically enabled in DEBUG builds.

endmenu
